# Mage

A turn-based grid roguelike where **movement is casting**. You never aim or select a
spell — every spell hangs off a trigger, so your turn is a routing decision: which path
through the crowd sets off the most magic.

Your weapon cuts across that: it fires every turn whatever you did, and rewards nothing.
**A step is a cast, a wait is a swing** — the same turn costs a mage everything and costs
a weapon-carrier nothing, and that difference is what a character is here.

Survive 400 turns.

Design: [DESIGN.md](./DESIGN.md) · Work breakdown: [tickets.md](./tickets.md) ·
